{"object":"How often a display can show a new image and the highest frame rate a liquid-crystal display can show.","predicate":"limits","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Refresh_rate","subject":"display refresh rate","text":"Refresh rate is how many times per second a display shows a new image, and for liquid-crystal displays it determines the highest frame rate that can be displayed. A console's 120 FPS capability therefore does not prove that an unverified television can show 120 distinct frames per second.","title":"prop_refresh_rate_limit"}